{
  "_note": "PLACEHOLDER \u2014 Claude-invented stopgaps for v0 feel, not balance; the whole vocabulary is being replaced by pressure sigils. THREE RULES WORTH KEEPING THROUGH THAT REWRITE: (1) 'stabilityDelta' is in the SAME UNITS as the Stability headline and simply adds to it \u2014 a book starts at 100 and a symbol reading '+12' moves it by exactly 12. (2) Stability tracks DEVIATION FROM WHAT A WORLD WOULD NATURALLY HAVE: asking for less than the baseline CALMS a world (Sparse Ore is +10), asking for the baseline costs nothing (Ore is 0), asking for more is the greed that destabilises (Rich Ore is \u221245). This is the Mystcraft greed model from research-pass-3, and it means the bounty slot is a real choice rather than a tax. (3) EVERY symbol trades on SEVERAL axes, never one: Dim Sky buys stability with sight and with things that hunt in the dark; Plains is stability-neutral but lets you see further. A stable world is not an empty one. 'expandsTo' spells the symbol out in the pressure model's atomic vocabulary \u2014 the rune spec calls these compounds (\u00a79). PLACEHOLDER component choices.",
